; OxCaml patch: upstream generates GIT-VERSION with an OCaml-syntax dune file
; (running "git describe" via Jbuild_plugin). Dune evaluates such files with
; the "ocaml" program from the build context, which does not exist in the
; oxcaml bootstrap contexts (their PATH starts with _build/_bootinstall/bin,
; which only contains the freshly built compilers). Use a static rule instead;
; an empty GIT-VERSION makes version.ml.in fall back to the plain VERSION,
; exactly like an upstream release tarball.

(rule
 (target GIT-VERSION)
 (action
  (with-stdout-to
   %{target}
   (echo ""))))
